<title>JAPAN: Japan Sept nickel imports fall 26.6 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Sept nickel imports fall 26.6 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's refined nickel imports totalled 3,793 tonnes in September, off 26.6 percent from 5,165 tonnes in the same month a year earlier, Finance Ministry data released on Tuesday showed.</p>
<p>Details were as follows (on a customs-cleared basis, in</p>
<p>tonnes):</p>
<p>		  Sept 96	Aug 96	Sept 95</p>
<p> Total	   3,793	  3,627	 5,165</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> Russia	    595	    601	 2,154</p>
<p> S. Africa	 210	    265	   278</p>
<p> Zimbabwe	  484	    354	   688</p>
<p>Imports in the first nine months of 1996 totalled 41,481</p>
<p>tonnes, against 53,982 tonnes in the same period the previous year. -- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
</text>
